- @root: Return

@one_nation
title: A speech on One Nation
subtitle: The wets and working-class voters are reassured. The dries suspect a coded attack.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; wet_dissent -= 6; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); de_con += 1*(1-dissent); dry_dissent += 3

Gilmour reminds the party that Disraeli wanted to unite the two nations, not to choose between them. The speech is reported as a rebuke. He insists it isn't.

@defence
title: Back the armed forces
view-if: con_in_government = 0
subtitle: The right and the services approve.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; right_dissent -= 4; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); labour_credibility -= 1

Gilmour attacks Labour's defence cuts and promises the forces a pay rise. Even the right has to admit he does it well.

@europe
title: Negotiate with our European partners
view-if: con_in_government = 1
subtitle: Better relations with Europe, and progress on the budget rebate.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; europe_relation += 8; eec_rebate += 1 if eec_rebate = 1; wet_dissent -= 2; right_dissent += 3

Gilmour and Carrington spend a long weekend in Brussels. [? if eec_rebate = 2 : They come back with a deal on the rebate that you think is too generous to the Community and everyone else thinks is a triumph. ?][? if eec_rebate < 2 : They come back with goodwill rather than money. ?]

@temper
title: Temper the monetarists in Cabinet
view-if: con_in_government = 1
subtitle: Cabinet tension falls. The dries resent it.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; cabinet_revolt -= 1; wet_dissent -= 4; dry_dissent += 5; economic_liberalism -= 1

Gilmour argues, at length and with footnotes, that the money supply figures mean nothing. The wets feel they have a champion at the table.
